# The tone, the quality of a vibe's experience, the first base element. It is the ternary value with three cases: a low value, a middle value, and a high value. Three is forced. The smallest usable alphabet needs a resting middle value and a mirror that swaps the two sides, and the three-case set is the smallest with both.
load @term/form/code/atom/flag
  find flag
  find either

form tone
  case low
  case middle
  case high

# The tone is ternary, proof-checked by `seed test`: three cases, a resting middle and a mirrored pair around it. Three
# is the smallest alphabet with both a middle and a mirror: 3 = 1 + 2.
hold tone-has-three-cases
  call is-equal
    code 3
    call add
      code 1
      code 2

# mirror swaps the two outer values around the resting middle: low and high trade places, middle is fixed. This is the
# reflection that, with the ternary set, makes three the smallest alphabet carrying both a center and a symmetry.
task mirror
  take t, like tone
  like tone
  fork case, read t
    case low
      send back
        make high
    case middle
      send back
        make middle
    case high
      send back
        make low

# The mirror is an INVOLUTION: mirror (mirror t) = t, for every tone. Reflecting twice returns the original value, so the
# symmetry is its own inverse, an order-two operation. Proved by case analysis on the three tones, each closing by
# computation. A reversible rule is built from order-two pieces, and this is the first of them.
rule mirror-tone-is-involution
  mark t, like tone
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mirror
        call mirror
          read t
      read t
  fold t

# The middle is the unique FIXED POINT of the mirror: mirror middle = middle. The resting value reflects to itself, which
# is why it is the neutral charge.
rule mirror-fixes-middle
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mirror
        make middle
      make middle
  calm hold

# The two outer tones are genuinely SWAPPED, not fixed: mirror low = high. With the fixed middle, this shows the mirror is
# the transposition of the outer pair, the order-two symmetry of the ternary set.
rule mirror-swaps-low-to-high
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mirror
        make low
      make high
  calm hold

# The charge sign: a tone reads as a signed value through the lean. The low value is negative, the middle is neutral, the
# high value is positive. This is the smallest signed group, the integers modulo their order: minus, naught, plus.
form spin
  case minus
  case naught
  case plus

# Negation of a sign flips minus and plus and fixes naught, exactly mirroring the tone reflection.
task flip-spin
  take s, like spin
  like spin
  fork case, read s
    case minus
      send back
        make plus
    case naught
      send back
        make naught
    case plus
      send back
        make minus

# The charge of a tone: low is minus, middle is naught, high is plus. This is how the lean turns a tone into a signed
# charge, the second base element acting on the first.
task charge
  take t, like tone
  like spin
  fork case, read t
    case low
      send back
        make minus
    case middle
      send back
        make naught
    case high
      send back
        make plus

# The mirror NEGATES charge: charge (mirror t) = flip-spin (charge t), for every tone. Reflecting a tone flips the sign of
# its charge, so the tone reflection IS sign negation carried back to the ternary value. The first base element and its
# order on the second are bound: the mirror is an order-two symmetry precisely because sign negation is.
rule mirror-negates-charge
  mark t, like tone
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call charge
        call mirror
          read t
      call flip-spin
        call charge
          read t
  fold t

# Sign negation is itself an INVOLUTION: flip-spin (flip-spin s) = s. The signed-charge group is order two, the same shape
# as the tone reflection, confirming the bridge above is an isomorphism of order-two symmetries.
rule flip-spin-is-involution
  mark s, like spin
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call flip-spin
        call flip-spin
          read s
      read s
  fold s

# A line, the unit the law acts on: two opposite sites of a dock, each carrying one tone, meeting head on. The knit's
# collide step rearranges the pair, and the stream step is the exchange across the line. Modelling the line here, where
# the tone constructors live, lets the law's reversibility and charge conservation be proved. It is a pairing of two tones.
form line
  case pair
    link head, like tone
    link tail, like tone

# The collide step, the actual knit collision table from the model: a fixed permutation of the nine line states that
# preserves the pair's signed sum. The two equal-pole pairs are inert. A pole meeting peace hops past it. A pole meeting
# its opposite annihilates to two peaces, peace meeting peace creates an opposite pole pair, and a pole pair flips, the
# neutral three-cycle peace-peace, high-low, low-high. Charge-conserving and reversible, with no adjustable parts.
# TEMPLATE: one row of a nine-state line table that outputs a line. For a fixed head tone, give the resulting head and
# tail tone against each of the three tail tones. One definition serves both the collide step and its inverse.
tree line-row
  take head-tone
  take low-head
  take low-tail
  take middle-head
  take middle-tail
  take high-head
  take high-tail

  hook fuse
    case {head-tone}
      fork case, read tail
        case low
          send back
            make pair
              bind head
                make {low-head}
              bind tail
                make {low-tail}
        case middle
          send back
            make pair
              bind head
                make {middle-head}
              bind tail
                make {middle-tail}
        case high
          send back
            make pair
              bind head
                make {high-head}
              bind tail
                make {high-tail}

# TEMPLATE: one row of a nine-state line table that outputs a single value. For a fixed head tone, give the value
# against each tail tone.
tree value-row
  take head-tone
  take at-low
  take at-middle
  take at-high

  hook fuse
    case {head-tone}
      fork case, read tail
        case low
          send back
            make {at-low}
        case middle
          send back
            make {at-middle}
        case high
          send back
            make {at-high}


task collide
  take l, like line
  like line
  fork case, read l
    case pair
      link head
      link tail
      fork case, read head
        fuse line-row, low, low, low, middle, low, middle, middle
        fuse line-row, middle, low, middle, high, low, high, middle
        fuse line-row, high, low, high, middle, high, high, high

# The inverse collision, the permutation run backward. Since the neutral three-cycle is not order two, reversibility is
# shown by an explicit inverse rather than by self-composition. Every other line state is fixed or in a two-cycle.
task uncollide
  take l, like line
  like line
  fork case, read l
    case pair
      link head
      link tail
      fork case, read head
        fuse line-row, low, low, low, middle, low, high, low
        fuse line-row, middle, low, middle, low, high, high, middle
        fuse line-row, high, middle, middle, middle, high, high, high

# The signed charge of a line: the sum of its two tone charges, a value in minus two to plus two. This is the quantity the
# collision must conserve, the discrete charge the law never creates or destroys.
form tally
  case sink-two
  case sink-one
  case flat
  case lift-one
  case lift-two

# The pair charge, tone plus tone read as a tally: the signed sum the lean assigns to a whole line.
task pair-charge
  take l, like line
  like tally
  fork case, read l
    case pair
      link head
      link tail
      fork case, read head
        fuse value-row, low, sink-two, sink-one, flat
        fuse value-row, middle, sink-one, flat, lift-one
        fuse value-row, high, flat, lift-one, lift-two

# The collide step is REVERSIBLE: uncollide (collide (pair a b)) = pair a b, for every pair of tones. The law of motion is
# invertible, so from the result of a beat the state before it is recovered and no information is lost. Proved by
# simultaneous case analysis on the two tones, all nine line states resolving by computation. This is the knit's first
# hard constraint, the reason any arrow of time must come from the growing edge and not from the local law.
rule collide-is-reversible
  mark a, like tone
  mark b, like tone
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call uncollide
        call collide
          make pair
            bind head
              read a
            bind tail
              read b
      make pair
        bind head
          read a
        bind tail
          read b
  fold a, b

# The collide step CONSERVES CHARGE: pair-charge (collide (pair a b)) = pair-charge (pair a b). The signed sum of the two
# tones is the same before and after the collision, across all nine line states. This is the knit's second hard
# constraint, the discrete conservation law from which the gauge charge and its current later emerge.
rule collide-conserves-charge
  mark a, like tone
  mark b, like tone
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call pair-charge
        call collide
          make pair
            bind head
              read a
            bind tail
              read b
      call pair-charge
        make pair
          bind head
            read a
          bind tail
            read b
  fold a, b

# The lean's order: low at the bottom, middle in the middle, high at the top. at-most a b is yes when a sits no higher
# than b. This is the order that turns a tone into a signed charge and gives growth its outward direction.
task at-most
  take a, like tone
  take b, like tone
  like flag
  fork case, read a
    case low
      send back
        make yes
    case middle
      fork case, read b
        case low
          send back
            make no
        case middle
          send back
            make yes
        case high
          send back
            make yes
    case high
      fork case, read b
        case low
          send back
            make no
        case middle
          send back
            make no
        case high
          send back
            make yes

# The order is REFLEXIVE: at-most t t = yes, every tone sits no higher than itself. By case on t.
rule at-most-is-reflexive
  mark t, like tone
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read t
        read t
      make yes
  fold t

# The order is TOTAL: either (at-most a b) (at-most b a) = yes, any two tones are comparable one way or the other. By
# simultaneous case analysis on both tones, the nine pairs each resolving by computation. With reflexivity this makes the
# lean a genuine total order on the ternary value.
rule at-most-is-total
  mark a, like tone
  mark b, like tone
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call either
        call at-most
          read a
          read b
        call at-most
          read b
          read a
      make yes
  fold a, b

# The order is ANTISYMMETRIC: if a is at most b AND b is at most a, then a = b. The two outer tones cannot each sit no
# higher than the other unless they are the same. Proved by simultaneous case analysis on both tones; the off-diagonal
# pairs are ruled out because one of the two hypotheses is false there, leaving only the equal cases.
rule at-most-is-antisymmetric
  mark a, like tone
  mark b, like tone
  have hab
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read a
        read b
      make yes
  have hba
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read b
        read a
      make yes
  show hold
    call is-equal
      read a
      read b
  fold a, b

# The order is TRANSITIVE: if a is at most b AND b is at most c, then a is at most c. The order carries through the
# middle. Proved by simultaneous case analysis on all three tones; impossible antecedent combinations are discharged.
rule at-most-is-transitive
  mark a, like tone
  mark b, like tone
  mark c, like tone
  have hab
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read a
        read b
      make yes
  have hbc
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read b
        read c
      make yes
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read a
        read c
      make yes
  fold a, b, c
